</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p5.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;">Supplementary Material for “<span id="p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Improving Reasoning for Diffusion Language Models via Group Diffusion Policy Optimization</span>”<span id="p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p6.1" class="ltx_p">In this supplementary material, we present additional details on variance decomposition in §<span id="p6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">A</span>, provide a theoretical analysis of asymptotic error bounds in §<span id="p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">B</span>, justify key properties of the integrand in §<span id="p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">C</span>, describe the experimental setup in §<span id="p6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">D</span>, and include representative generated samples in §<span id="p6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">E</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>More Details on Variance decomposition</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start by studying the different sources of variance in approximating the ELBO, in the case of masked diffusion models the equation is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right]\leq\log\pi(y|q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right]\leq\log\pi(y|q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From looking at this expression we observe that there are two sources of variance, <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Time Sampling:</span> we must sample <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> which determines the noise level, and <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Random Masking:</span> we must sample <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> which injects noise to the clean <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by analyzing how each source of randomness affects the variance of an estimator. To simplify our discussion, we will rewrite the integrand in a simplified way:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(x_{t}|y)}\left[Z(t,x_{t})\right]\leq\log\pi(y|q)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(x_{t}|y)}\left[Z(t,x_{t})\right]\leq\log\pi(y|q),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z(t,y_{t}):=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(t,y_{t}):=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable w.r.t. the joint distribution of <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. We are interested in studying <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}(Z(t,y_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}(Z(t,y_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> and how it decomposes with respect to <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, by the law of total variance we can decompose this as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Var}(Z(t,y_{t}))=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t}\!\left[\text{Var}(Z\mid t)\right]}_{\text{Var given by }Z|t}\;+\;\underbrace{\text{Var}_{t}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[Z\mid t]\right)}_{\text{Var given by }t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var given by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mtext>Var</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Var given by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Var}(Z(t,y_{t}))=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t}\!\left[\text{Var}(Z\mid t)\right]}_{\text{Var given by }Z|t}\;+\;\underbrace{\text{Var}_{t}\!\left(\mathbb{E}[Z\mid t]\right)}_{\text{Var given by }t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The above expression indicates that we can understand variance as the sum of two components, where each term corresponds to a distinct source of variance. We argue that most of the variance comes from selecting the noise level <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. When the noise level is <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> we range from fully unmasked to fully masked, creating a large disparity in the noise samples and subsequently causing large swings in the variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To test this we evaluate each term in <a href="#A1.E9" title="In Appendix A More Details on Variance decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> for <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> different prompts pulled from the OpenWeb dataset. We plot the mean and variance as function of time in Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Disentangling Variance in ELBO ‣ 3 Improving Reasoning via Group Diffusion Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. This figure reveals very important facts:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most of the variance is coming from randomly selecting the timestamps/ noise levels and not from injecting noise into the text.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The loss function when observed as a function of time yields a simple structure.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For this reason, we advocate for <em id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fixed timestamps</em> for likelihood approximation and embracing a <em id="A1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Semi-deterministic Monte Carlo sampler</em> instead of the naïve double Monte Carlo approximations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the error bound of approximating the ELBO via the proposed Semi-Deterministic Monte Carlo scheme, focusing on the training objective given in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E2" title="In Denoising objective. ‣ 2.1 Masked Diffusion Language Models (MDMs) ‣ 2 Preliminaries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), namely,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation and definition.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed by first defining the relevant quantities that will be used in the ensuing technical analysis. Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{t}:=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}:=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is a <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">random variable</span> with respect to the distribution of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot|y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g(t):=\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot\,|y)}(Z_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t):=\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi_{t}(\cdot\,|y)}(Z_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the Monte Carlo approximation of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\text{MC}}(t):=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}(Z_{t}^{[k]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\text{MC}}(t):=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}(Z_{t}^{[k]})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}^{[k]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}^{[k]}</annotation></semantics></math> are iid draws of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. For convenience, we let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}(y_{t}):=\{i\in\{1,\cdots,L\}:y_{t}^{i}=M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(y_{t}):=\{i\in\{1,\cdots,L\}:y_{t}^{i}=M\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}=|\mathcal{I}(y_{t})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}=|\mathcal{I}(y_{t})|</annotation></semantics></math>, the cardinality of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}(y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be rewritten as <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}\equiv\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}(t)}\log p_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}\equiv\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}(t)}\log p_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With these definitions, the training objective of interest is given by</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\big(g(t)\big)=\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\big(g(t)\big)=\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and its approximation via a Semi-deterministic Monte Carlo scheme (namely, Eq.(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.3 Variance Reduction via Semi-deterministic Monte Carlo ‣ 3 Improving Reasoning via Group Diffusion Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)) can be written as</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q):=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q):=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which is a numerical approximation of the integral in the Monte Carlo approximation <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q):=\int_{0}^{1}g_{\text{MC}}\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q):=\int_{0}^{1}g_{\text{MC}}\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math> at points <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n},n=1,\cdots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n},n=1,\cdots,N</annotation></semantics></math>. For the time being, we assume a generic numerical approximation of the integral, and using the notation involving <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The approximation error of Eq.(<a href="#A2.E12" title="In Notation and definition. ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is given by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left(\left[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}-\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}\right]^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left(\left[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}-\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}\right]^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t\right]^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t\right]^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\right)^{2}\right]}_{\text{MC variance}}+\underbrace{\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\right)^{2}}_{\text{integration bias}^{2}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>MC variance</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mtext>integration bias</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\right)^{2}\right]}_{\text{MC variance}}+\underbrace{\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\right)^{2}}_{\text{integration bias}^{2}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">this holds due to the independence of Monte Carlo samples, since</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\biggl[\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})\biggr]=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\mathbb{E}[g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})]=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\biggl[\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})\biggr]=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\mathbb{E}[g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})]=\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and therefore the second term boils down to the integration bias. It can be seen that this becomes the classical mean-squared-error of an estimator, which can be decomposed into the variance (from a total of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> Monte Carlo samples) and the bias<sup id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> (from the approximation of the integral) at <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> points <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},\cdots,t_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},\cdots,t_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounds of these two terms will be analyzed separately in the sequel.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>The variance term</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze this term, we start with the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pointwise</span> Monte Carlo error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">C1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t})&lt;\infty,\quad\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t}^{2})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t})&lt;\infty,\quad\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t}^{2})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">C2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\ \delta&gt;0:\delta&lt;\ \pi_{\theta}(y^{i}\mid y_{t},q)&lt;1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∃</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.778em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\ \delta&gt;0:\delta&lt;\ \pi_{\theta}(y^{i}\mid y_{t},q)&lt;1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for all </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the following holds</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\biggl(g(t)-g_{\text{MC}}(t)\biggr)^{2}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t),\qquad\text{where}\quad\sigma^{2}(t):=\text{Var}(Z_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\biggl(g(t)-g_{\text{MC}}(t)\biggr)^{2}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t),\qquad\text{where}\quad\sigma^{2}(t):=\text{Var}(Z_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish the results in Eq.(<a href="#A2.E14" title="In Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), the following assumptions need to hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">A1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Measurability: <math id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is jointly measurable in <math id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">A2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Integrability: <math id="A2.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(|Z_{t}|)&lt;\infty,\ \forall\ t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(|Z_{t}|)&lt;\infty,\ \forall\ t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">A3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finite variance: <math id="A2.I2.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t)&lt;\infty,\ \forall\ t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t)&lt;\infty,\ \forall\ t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By writing <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}(y_{t})}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}\mid y_{t},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}(y_{t})}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}\mid y_{t},q)</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be verified that C1 and C2 are sufficient for A1-A3 to hold.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Interpretation of conditions C1 and C2 are given as follows: C1 requires the number of masked tokens to be controlled, and C2 requires the conditional likelihood to be well behaved.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Coming back to the variance term, by Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, at each time point <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>’s), the Monte Carlo estimate <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> introduces random error whose pointwise variance is given by <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the variance of the estimator <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{ELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\Big(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\underbrace{\big(g(t_{n})-g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})\big)}_{:=u_{n}}\Big)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>MC</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\Big(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\underbrace{\big(g(t_{n})-g_{\text{MC}}(t_{n})\big)}_{:=u_{n}}\Big)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}u_{n}\big)^{2}=\frac{1}{K}\biggl(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\biggr);" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}u_{n}\big)^{2}=\frac{1}{K}\biggl(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\biggr);</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">the last equality holds since for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}\neq t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}\neq t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, due to the independence of MC samples across <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}(u_{n},u_{m})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}(u_{n},u_{m})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>; further note that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(u_{n})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(u_{n})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}u_{n}^{2}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}u_{n}^{2}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmproposition1" title="Proposition B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> shows that under a refinement of condition C1, Eq.(<a href="#A2.E15" title="In B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) is bounded and therefore its rate can be derived accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the following condition holds for <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (defined identically to that in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>):</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">C1’.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t})\leq C_{0}t^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c_{t})\leq C_{0}t^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some constant </span><math id="A2.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume also that <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are approximately equally spaced. Then, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w^{2}_{n}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C_{0}}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w^{2}_{n}t_{n}=O\big(\frac{1}{K}\cdot\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{N}t_{n}\big)=O\big(\frac{1}{K}\frac{1}{N^{2}}N\int_{0}^{1}t\mathrm{d}t\big)=O\Big(\frac{1}{KN}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>N</mi><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w^{2}_{n}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C_{0}}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w^{2}_{n}t_{n}=O\big(\frac{1}{K}\cdot\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sum_{n=1}^{N}t_{n}\big)=O\big(\frac{1}{K}\frac{1}{N^{2}}N\int_{0}^{1}t\mathrm{d}t\big)=O\Big(\frac{1}{KN}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Condition C1’ guarantees that <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}\sigma^{2}(t)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}\sigma^{2}(t)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, which then implies the finiteness of <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, provided that the weights <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a valid integration scheme; i.e., <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the mesh of the points <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes finer as <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Empirically, C1’ can be operationalized by considering a masking scheme where token <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is masked independently across <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\cdots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\cdots,L</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}\sim\mathsf{Bin}(L,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}\sim\mathsf{Bin}(L,t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the assumption on weights <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}=O(\frac{1}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}=O(\frac{1}{N})</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="A2.Thmremark2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>’s being roughly equally spaced are both fairly reasonable for all integration schemes (simple Riemann, midpoint, trapezoid, Simpson).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The next proposition shows that when an <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent decay condition is satisfied by the log-likelihood, then a rate faster than the one established in Eq.(<a href="#A2.E16" title="In Proposition B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) can be obtained.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the following condition holds</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">C1”.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c^{2}_{t})\leq C_{\text{token}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">token</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}}(c^{2}_{t})\leq C_{\text{token}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I4.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some positive constant </span><math id="A2.I4.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{token}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">token</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{token}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I4.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition, assume the log-likelihood satisfies the following, for some positive constant <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{log-lik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">log-lik</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{log-lik}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}\big(\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\big)\leq C_{\text{log-lik}}\frac{t^{2}}{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">log-lik</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}\big(\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\big)\leq C_{\text{log-lik}}\frac{t^{2}}{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the following holds</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})=O\left(\frac{1}{KN^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})=O\left(\frac{1}{KN^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given the definition of <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (see, e.g., Eq.(<a href="#A2.E14" title="In Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1 The variance term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>)), under condition C1”, one has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t)\leq\frac{\text{C}^{2}_{\text{token}}}{t^{2}}\text{Var}\big(\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>token</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t)\leq\frac{\text{C}^{2}_{\text{token}}}{t^{2}}\text{Var}\big(\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for weights <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{n}w_{n}=O(\frac{1}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{n}w_{n}=O(\frac{1}{N})</annotation></semantics></math> (which are the weights for all standard integration rules) and <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}=\frac{n}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}=\frac{n}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C^{2}_{\text{token}}}{t_{n}^{2}}C_{\text{log-lik}}\frac{t_{n}^{2}}{N}=C_{0}\frac{1}{N},\quad\text{where}~C_{0}=C^{2}_{\text{token}}C_{\text{log-lik}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mtext>token</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>log-lik</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mtext>token</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>log-lik</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C^{2}_{\text{token}}}{t_{n}^{2}}C_{\text{log-lik}}\frac{t_{n}^{2}}{N}=C_{0}\frac{1}{N},\quad\text{where}~C_{0}=C^{2}_{\text{token}}C_{\text{log-lik}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we have a uniform bound on <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq C_{0}\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq C_{0}\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,\cdots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,\cdots,N</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the above uniform bound, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C_{0}}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}=\frac{C_{0}}{N}\biggl[N\frac{1}{N^{2}}\biggr]=\frac{C_{0}}{N^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})\leq\frac{C_{0}}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}=\frac{C_{0}}{N}\biggl[N\frac{1}{N^{2}}\biggr]=\frac{C_{0}}{N^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})=O\left(\frac{1}{KN^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}^{2}\sigma^{2}(t_{n})=O\left(\frac{1}{KN^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Some intuition behind the <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent decay condition is given as follows. Specifically, for the log-likelihood to satisfy such a condition, one compatible specification is given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)=h(t)+\frac{t}{\sqrt{N}}\epsilon_{t},~~\text{where}~~~~\mathbb{E}(\epsilon_{t})=0,~~\text{Var}(\epsilon_{t})\leq\sigma_{0}~\text{for some $\sigma_{0}&gt;0$};\quad\forall t;" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1.32em;" width="1.32em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>for some </mtext><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)=h(t)+\frac{t}{\sqrt{N}}\epsilon_{t},~~\text{where}~~~~\mathbb{E}(\epsilon_{t})=0,~~\text{Var}(\epsilon_{t})\leq\sigma_{0}~\text{for some $\sigma_{0}&gt;0$};\quad\forall t;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth Lipschitz function. Under this specification, the fluctuation of the likelihood is small for small <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (little masking) and increases for large <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>The bias term</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we analyze the bias term induced by approximating the integral <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math> via numerical integration schemes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma provides the rate of the bias for the case where some quadrature rule is used, under certain assumptions of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t):(0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t):(0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic and continuously twice differentiable function (i.e., in <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>). Further, suppose we use some quadrature rule (midpoint, trapezoidal, Simpson, etc.) to approximate its integral at points <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{n}\}_{n=1}^{N}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{n}\}_{n=1}^{N}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\approx\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\approx\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where weights <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are chosen according to the specific quadrature rule in use. Then, such an approximation scheme introduces deterministic integration bias, given by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{N}(g)=\mid\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\mid," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{N}(g)=\mid\int_{0}^{1}g(t)\mathrm{d}t-\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})\mid,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and it scales as follows:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for midpoint or trapezoidal rule, as </span><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{N^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{N^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for Simpson, as </span><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{N^{4}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{N^{4}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">These are standard results from numerical analysis; see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dahlquist and Björck (2008)</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Atkinson (2008)</a></cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The above lemma directly yields the following result: for the integration bias<sup id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> that appears in the decomposition of Eq.(<a href="#A2.E13" title="In Notation and definition. ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), it follows that for midpoint or trapezoidal rule,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\right)^{2}=O(\frac{1}{N^{4}});" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}g(t_{n})-\int_{0}^{1}g(t)dt\right)^{2}=O(\frac{1}{N^{4}});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and for Simpson, the rate is given by <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{N^{8}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{N^{8}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above rates suggest that by applying a quadrature rule—provided that <math id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies certain properties—the integration bias<sup id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> has become practically negligible, relative to the variance term that dominates. However, if one uses a generic integration scheme instead, such as the Riemann sum, the integration bias would scale at the rate of <math id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{N})</annotation></semantics></math> and thus the bias<sup id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> at <math id="A2.Thmremark3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{N^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{N^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As it can be seen from Remark <a href="#A2.Thmremark3" title="Remark B.3. ‣ B.2 The bias term ‣ Appendix B Analysis of Asymptotic Error Bounds" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, the “gain" by considering a Semi-Deterministic Monte Carlo scheme is partly built on the fact that the integration bias<sup id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> can be practically negligible, which hinges on whether one can use quadrature rules for integration. However, to apply such rules, <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be continuously twice differentiable, and its properties are further studied in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this section, we will denote <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> a probability distribution on <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> marginal of the forward process under masked diffusion and <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the learned marginal. Our goal is to state some conditions under which the loss function would be well-suited for numerical quadratures. We start by noting that from Proposition 1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benton et al. (2024)</a></cite> we can write the ELBO in the following form:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(y|q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{y_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|y)}\left[\frac{1}{t}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathbf{1}[y_{t}^{i}=M]\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{i}|y_{t},q)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\Phi\left(\frac{p_{t}(y)}{\pi_{t}(y_{t})}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[\Phi\left(\frac{p_{t}(y)}{\pi_{t}(y_{t})}\right)\right]\mathrm{d}t+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})\mathrm{d}t+C," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})\mathrm{d}t+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the score matching operator introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benton et al. (2024)</a></cite>. This calculation allows to realize that to study the integrand it is enough to study <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})=:f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})=:f(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that with this definition, the integrand <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in the previous section satisfies <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)=f^{\prime}(t)+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)=f^{\prime}(t)+C</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition (1.1) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benton et al. (2024)</a></cite> we know that <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation:</span> We first introduce the following notation: let <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability distribution <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> marginalized over the entries not in <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following lemma states that we can write <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as a polynomial with coefficients relating to the average <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> under different levels of masking.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence for two distributions over time evolving according to masked diffusion is <math id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of <math id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and we can write:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k}=\frac{1}{\binom{D}{k}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k}=\frac{1}{\binom{D}{k}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is the average <math id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence over sets of size <math id="A3.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof relies on fundamental combinatorial facts and the definition of the forward process:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in[M]^{D}}p_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{\pi_{t}(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in[M]^{D}}p_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{\pi_{t}(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}S\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}p_{t}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{\pi_{t}(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}S\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}p_{t}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{\pi_{t}(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}{t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}{t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}{\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}x:x_{i}=M\\
\iff i\in S\end{subarray}}p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)\log\!\left(\frac{p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}{\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using this, we can rewrite the <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}||\pi_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{S}\subset[D]\\
|\mathcal{S}|=k\end{subarray}}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which gives the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Given this lemma, it becomes clear that to understand the properties of the integrand, it is enough to understand the following polynomial:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}\binom{D}{k}t^{k}(1-t)^{D-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}B_{k,D}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{D}c_{k}B_{k,D}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This is a Bernstein polynomial, and its properties have been studied before.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forward differences and Bernstein derivatives.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When looking at the derivatives of Bernestein polynomials, the differences of the coefficients appear; to this end denote:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{k+1}-c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{k+1}-c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{2}c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{2}c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{k+2}-2c_{k+1}+c_{k}=(c_{k+2}-c_{k+1})-(c_{k+1}-c_{k})=\Delta_{k+1}-\Delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{k+2}-2c_{k+1}+c_{k}=(c_{k+2}-c_{k+1})-(c_{k+1}-c_{k})=\Delta_{k+1}-\Delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{3}c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{3}c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{k+3}-3c_{k+2}+3c_{k+1}-c_{k}=\Delta_{k+1}^{2}-\Delta_{k}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{k+3}-3c_{k+2}+3c_{k+1}-c_{k}=\Delta_{k+1}^{2}-\Delta_{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then it is easy to check that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Derivative formulas)<span id="A3.Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A3.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D\sum_{k=0}^{D-1}\Delta c_{k}\,B_{k,D-1}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D\sum_{k=0}^{D-1}\Delta c_{k}\,B_{k,D-1}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{\prime\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{\prime\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D(D-1)\sum_{k=0}^{D-2}\Delta^{2}c_{k}\,B_{k,D-2}(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D(D-1)\sum_{k=0}^{D-2}\Delta^{2}c_{k}\,B_{k,D-2}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{(3)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{(3)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D(D-1)(D-2)\sum_{k=0}^{D-3}\Delta^{3}c_{k}\,B_{k,D-3}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D(D-1)(D-2)\sum_{k=0}^{D-3}\Delta^{3}c_{k}\,B_{k,D-3}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k,n}(t)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k,n}(t)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the signs of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(r)}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(r)}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are controlled by the signs of the averaged forward differences <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{r}c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{r}c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">One-step representation via KL chain rule.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F(\mathcal{S})=\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathcal{S})=\mathrm{KL}(p_{0}^{\mathcal{S}}||\pi_{0}^{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we are now able to obtain simple, intuitive explanations of the meaning of each coefficient <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the (nonnegative) one-step gain</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\;:=\;F(\mathcal{S}\cup\{i\})-F(\mathcal{S})=\mathbb{E}_{X_{\mathcal{S}}\sim P_{0}^{(\mathcal{S})}}\!\left[\mathrm{KL}\!\big(P_{0}(X_{i}\!\mid X_{\mathcal{S}})\,\|\,Q_{0}(X_{i}\!\mid X_{\mathcal{S}})\big)\right]\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\;:=\;F(\mathcal{S}\cup\{i\})-F(\mathcal{S})=\mathbb{E}_{X_{\mathcal{S}}\sim P_{0}^{(\mathcal{S})}}\!\left[\mathrm{KL}\!\big(P_{0}(X_{i}\!\mid X_{\mathcal{S}})\,\|\,Q_{0}(X_{i}\!\mid X_{\mathcal{S}})\big)\right]\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The above quantity represents the average <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> that we obtain by masking an extra token to a given set. Intuitively we expect <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to be increasing, as masking more tokens reduces the amount of information that we have (This in fact, holds already without extra assumptions). Similarly, we can obtain the iterated differences:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{2}c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{2}c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i,j\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i,j\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{3}c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{3}c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i,j,\ell\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j,\ell\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{\ell\})+\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}|\mathcal{S}|=k\\
i,j,\ell\notin\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\!\big[\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j,\ell\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{\ell\})+\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If such quantities are positive, this will immediately imply that the derivatives in <a href="#A3.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma C.2 (Derivative formulas). ‣ Forward differences and Bernstein derivatives. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> will be positive, implying important consequences on the loss function. Intuitively, such coefficients being positive correspond to the idea that masking one token when <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> are masked results in more loss of information than masking a token when <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&lt;K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&lt;K</annotation></semantics></math> are masked. We require these as assumptions and explain the sufficient conditions for them to hold in the following Proposition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sufficient conditions for convexity and increasing integrand)<span id="A3.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Integrand is positive</em><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) For any </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0},Q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0},Q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the set function </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is monotone:
</span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq T\Rightarrow F(\mathcal{S})\leq F(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq T\Rightarrow F(\mathcal{S})\leq F(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (data processing under marginalization).
Hence </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta c_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta c_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and by Eq.(</span><a href="#A3.E19" title="In Lemma C.2 (Derivative formulas). ‣ Forward differences and Bernstein derivatives. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{~f^{\prime}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{~f^{\prime}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Integrand is increasing in <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) If the </span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Increasing Conditional Divergence</span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (ICD) condition holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\ \leq\ \Delta_{i}(\mathcal{T})\qquad\text{for all }\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{T}\subseteq[D]\setminus\{i\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\ \leq\ \Delta_{i}(\mathcal{T})\qquad\text{for all }\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{T}\subseteq[D]\setminus\{i\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}c_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}c_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by Eq.(</span><a href="#A3.E23" title="In One-step representation via KL chain rule. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), and Eq.(</span><a href="#A3.E20" title="In Lemma C.2 (Derivative formulas). ‣ Forward differences and Bernstein derivatives. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{~f^{\prime\prime}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{~f^{\prime\prime}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}^{2}}{\mathrm{d}t^{2}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Integrand has convexity in <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) If, in addition, the </span><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">second-order ICD</span><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> condition holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big)\ \leq\ \big(\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j,\ell\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{\ell\})\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S})\big)\ \leq\ \big(\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{j,\ell\})-\Delta_{i}(\mathcal{S}\cup\{\ell\})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all distinct </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j,\ell</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subseteq[D]\setminus\{i,j,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subseteq[D]\setminus\{i,j,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{3}c_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{3}c_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by Eq.(</span><a href="#A3.E24" title="In One-step representation via KL chain rule. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), and Eq.(</span><a href="#A3.E21" title="In Lemma C.2 (Derivative formulas). ‣ Forward differences and Bernstein derivatives. ‣ Appendix C Properties of the integrand in the numerical quadrature" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{~f^{(3)}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}^{3}}{\mathrm{d}t^{3}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{~f^{(3)}(t)=\frac{\mathrm{d}^{3}}{\mathrm{d}t^{3}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{t}\|Q_{t})\ \geq\ 0~}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Empirical Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Training Details</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We leverage the codebase from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2025)</a></cite> which in itself leverages the TRL library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Werra et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. For our hyperparameters we keep most of the default parameters from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2025)</a></cite> without any hyperparameter search. We leverage a Low-Rank Adaptation with rank <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=128</annotation></semantics></math> and scaling factor <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=64</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Across all runs we utilize the AdamW optimizer with parameters <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math> with a weight decay of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient clipping at <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>. We leverage flash attention and <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4-</annotation></semantics></math>bit quantization. We found that GDPO usually requires a smaller learning rate than diffu-GRPO and otherwise it can result in diverging models. We save checkpoints every <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math> iterations and stop our runs when the reward function has plateaued, for the countdown dataset we observe that the reward function continuous increasing for a very long time, while for the math dataset we observed high-performing checkpoints around <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9000</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, but report the best one, which happened later in training. We present the learning rate as well as other hyperparameters in Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ D.1 Training Details ‣ Appendix D Empirical Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We present the reward function for the different datasets in Figure <a href="#A4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ D.1 Training Details ‣ Appendix D Empirical Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and observe that GDPO can offer a steady growth before plateauing.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08554v1/loss_math.svg" id="A4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/395;" width="476" height="395"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08554v1/loss_gsm8k.svg" id="A4.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/395;" width="476" height="395"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08554v1/loss_countdown.svg" id="A4.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/395;" width="476" height="395"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A4.F5.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="A4.F5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:345.0pt;"></span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08554v1/loss_sudoku.svg" id="A4.F5.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/395;" width="476" height="395"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F5.fig5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08554v1/loss_kodcode.svg" id="A4.F5.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/395;" width="476" height="395"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A4.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reward curves during RL training for the models reported in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A4.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters for different training runs</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T4.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;">
<span id="A4.T4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T4.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A4.T4.6.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Model</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A4.T4.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">GSM8K</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A4.T4.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">MATH500</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A4.T4.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Countdown</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.6.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:9.0pt;padding-right:9.0pt;"><span id="A4.T4.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sudoku</span></td>
